---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { Timeline } from '../components/home/Timeline';
import { SiteCredit } from '../components/SiteCredit';
import { url } from '../lib/paths';
---
<Base
  title="About this guide"
  description="An independent guide to the UN System Data Commons and the undata Python package: who made it, how the videos are made, and what the site stores."
  section="about"
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 pb-6 pt-8 sm:px-6 sm:pt-12">
    <h1 class="font-display text-h1 font-semibold text-ink-primary sm:text-display" data-pagefind-meta="title">About this guide</h1>
    <div class="mt-6 max-w-measure space-y-5 text-lead text-ink-secondary">
      <p>
        The UN System Data Commons at <a class="link" href="https://data.un.org" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">data.un.org</a>
        went live on 17 September 2026. It joins the public statistics of 26 UN System entities into one knowledge graph, free to
        use, with no login and no key. This guide teaches it in short videos: how to find a figure you can defend, and how to
        take it into Python, Excel, PowerPoint or an AI assistant with its source attached.
      </p>
      <p>
        It is an independent guide, not an official United Nations publication, and it is not endorsed by the United Nations or by
        Google. Every statistic belongs to the agency that published it and carries that agency's terms of use.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2 class="mt-12 font-display text-h2 font-semibold text-ink-primary">How the videos are made</h2>
    <ul class="mt-4 max-w-measure space-y-3 text-body text-ink-secondary">
      <li><strong class="text-ink-primary">No figure on screen was typed in by hand.</strong> The data.un.org videos are built from real pages of the platform, captured in a browser on 18 September 2026. In the undata videos, every number was returned by the package from the live platform, on the date each lesson shows.</li>
      <li><strong class="text-ink-primary">The tools are real too.</strong> In the "Present" lessons, Excel, PowerPoint and R draw the charts from the files undata saved. The Flourish race is a preview drawn from the same CSV, and the Copilot lesson shows a real reply from GPT-5.4, labelled with the model and the date.</li>
      <li><strong class="text-ink-primary">The voice is synthetic</strong> (Azure AI Speech), and the music and sound were made for the series. Every video has its captions burned in, and its full transcript on its lesson page.</li>
      <li><strong class="text-ink-primary">Each one lands one idea</strong> in under three minutes, so it can be watched before a meeting starts.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="mt-12 font-display text-h2 font-semibold text-ink-primary">Privacy: what this site stores</h2>
    <ul class="mt-4 max-w-measure space-y-3 text-body text-ink-secondary">
      <li>This site sets no cookies, has no accounts and runs no tracking scripts.</li>
      <li>Nothing loads from YouTube until you press play. The player is YouTube's privacy-enhanced one, which may then store its own data. Fonts and images are served by this site.</li>
      <li>Your progress through the lessons is kept in your browser and never leaves it. <button type="button" data-progress-clear class="link">Clear my progress</button></li>
      <li>The charts on the guide pages ask data.un.org for their figures directly from your browser. If it can't be reached, they show a snapshot stored with this site, and say so.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="mt-12 font-display text-h2 font-semibold text-ink-primary">Who made it</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-measure text-body text-ink-secondary">
      Mafizul Islam designed, wrote and built the guide, the videos and the undata package, as a
      <a class="link" href="https://nerd-factory.github.io/nerd-lab/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">Nerd Lab</a> project. The source is
      <a class="link" href="https://github.com/MafiAtUN/un-data-commons-field-guide" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">on GitHub</a>, and corrections are welcome as issues there.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-6"><SiteCredit /></div>
  </div>

  <div class="mx-auto mt-14 max-w-6xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <h2 class="font-display text-h2 font-semibold text-ink-primary">How data.un.org came about</h2>
    <p class="mt-2 max-w-measure text-body text-ink-secondary">
      Two threads: what the UN decided, and what the technology it now runs on could do. They meet in September 2026. Every date links to where it came from.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-6">
      <Timeline client:visible />
    </div>
    <p class="mt-8 text-body"><a class="link" href={url('/courses/')}>Back to the courses</a></p>
  </div>
</Base>
